  body: "# IB in youth: contribution and overlap classifications\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe source describes
    IB(Y) as an IB category that is not based on contribution conditions, while expressly treating it as contributory
    for the purpose of overlapping-benefit rules.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\n“Contributory” is purpose-specific
    here. Do not infer a contribution requirement from the overlap label or treat the label as an ontology-wide
    contradiction. Retained SDA, age, incapacity, residence and historical claim restrictions still matter.\n\n\
    ## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 56002, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a80bf45ed915d74e623036c/dmgch56.pdf#page=5).\n\
    - [DMG 56019, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a80bf45ed915d74e623036c/dmgch56.pdf#page=11).\n\
    - [DMG 56034, PDF page 16](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a80bf45ed915d74e623036c/dmgch56.pdf#page=16).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch56`:
    PDF `24fde3944e7e2605c24baf711da1ace4dfe0032fe13b6bfc169e4562bf5ecca5`; extracted pages `b5dc3260133af75807e6248202525da77a6610befc0b7ff20bc883d2ebba530e`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.379452Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a80bf45ed915d74e623036c/dmgch56.pdf#page=5
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-overlapping-benefits
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly gives IB(Y) a contributory classification only for overlapping-benefit
      purposes.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch56/0016
      quote: "56034   For the purpose of overlapping benefits IB is a contributory benefit. This applies\n     \
        \   even though IB(Y) is not based on contribution conditions. For the purpose of\n        overlapping benefits
        contributory benefits are those benefits prescribed in\n        legislation1.\n                        \
        \                                   1 SS (OB) Regs, reg 2(1); SS CB Act 92, Part 11\n\n\n        IB for
        person incapacitated in youth and CHB"
      locator: DMG 56034
  - target: term/sda-continuation-boundary
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source excludes IB(Y) where SDA entitlement is retained; this is not equivalence of
      benefits.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch56/0011
      quote: "56019   The conditions for receiving IB(Y), including the age conditions, are set out in DMG\n   \
        \     56020. In some circumstances the upper age condition can be extended (see DMG\n        56023). In
        some circumstances a person who does not satisfy the upper age\n        condition can be entitled to IB
        because of previous entitlement to IB(Y) (see DMG\n        56031).\n\n        Note: A person who retains
        entitlement to SDA (see DMG Chapter 57) has no\n        entitlement to IB(Y)."
      locator: DMG 56019
